Room: Splunk: Exploring SPL
For first question "What is the name of the host in the Data Summary tab?" answer is "cyber-host". To get that I wrote in search head "index=windowslogs" and changed the time to "Al Time" in "Other". After that, in the "Selected Filds" I chose "host" and saw "cyber-host". That is the name of the host, which is the case of alerts. (images/Screenshot 2026-02-05 212119.png)  
In the search History, what is the 7th search query in the list? (excluding your searches from today). The answer is index=windowslogs | chart count(EventCode) by Image, this can we see in the first tab Search History of Search & Reporting.
In the left field panel, which Source IP has recorded max events? The answer is 172.90.12.11. In the left field find the SourceAddress, we can see values, which contain this IP address. Another IP 0.0.0.0 uses for all networks. And 127.0.0.1 - this is loopback, which uses for test network programs.
How many events are returned when we apply the time filter to display events on 04/15/2022 and Time from 08:05 AM to 08:06 AM? The answer is 134. We can use in the search head additional string - earliest="04/15/2022:08:05:00" latest="04/15/2022:08:06:00".
How many Events are returned when searching for Event ID 1 AND User as *James*? The answer is index=windowslogs EventID=1 AND User=*James* for that we use search head and returned 4.
How many events are observed with Destination IP 172.18.39.6 AND destination Port 135? The answer is index=windowslogs DestinationIp=172.18.39.6 AND DestinationPort=135 for that we use search head and returned 4.
What is the Source IP with highest count returned with this Search query? Search Query: index=windowslogs  Hostname="Salena.Adam" DestinationIp="172.18.38.5". I use this and create the search query: index=windowslogs Hostname="Salena.Adam" AND DestinationIp="172.18.38.5" and in the left panel we can see SourceIp field, the first value is the answer it is 172.90.12.11.
In the index windowslogs, search for all the events that contain the term cyber how many events returned? The answer is index=windowslogs cyber and returned 0.
Now search for the term cyber*, how many events are returned? The answer is index=windowslogs cyber* and returned 12256.
What is the third EventID returned against this search query? We can use the search queary to get the answer index=windowslogs |  table_time EventID Hostname SourceName | reverse. The answer is 4103 of third event.
Use the dedup command against the Hostname field before the reverse command in the query mentioned in Question 1. What is the first username returned in the Hostname field? Using dedup for this search queary and get index=windowslogs |  table_time EventID Hostname SourceName | dedup Hostname| reverse. The answer is Salena.Adam.
Using the Reverse command with the search query index=windowslogs | table _time EventID Hostname SourceName - what is the HostName that comes on top? The answer is James.browne. For this we use this search query + | reverse in the end.
What is the last EventID returned when the query in question 1 is updated with the tail command? The answer is 4103. We use for that this search queary index=windowslogs | table _time EventID Hostname SourceName | tail (in the end add | tail, which returns last 10 events in the list).
Sort the above query against the SourceName. What is the top SourceName returned? The answer is Microsoft-Windows-Directory-Services-SAM. For that we use search queary index=windowslogs | table _time EventID Hostname SourceName | sort SourceName.
List the top 8 Image processes using the top command -  what is the total count of the 6th Image? We use this search queary - index=windowslogs | top limit=8 Image. And the answer is 196 of the 6th Image.
Using the rare command, identify the user with the least number of activities captured? We use this search queary - index=windowslogs | rare User, because we need to find User so using this field. The answer is James. 
Create a pie-chart using the chart command - what is the count for the conhost.exe process? The answer is 70. We use this search queary - index=windowslogs | chart count by Image, because Image is responsible for process that happend in the system.

